      "correct": 3,
      "explanation": "Print Spooler is the Windows service that queues and dispatches print jobs. If it is stopped or hung, use Services or Task Manager’s Services tab to start or restart it with suitable authorization. Restarting the service is a targeted step before reinstalling the printer when the service is the identified cause. Processes > End task, Startup apps, and Performance are not the proper service-control action. Persistent jobs may require an approved queue-clearing procedure after stopping the spooler; do not delete arbitrary user data or format the system.",
