      "explanation": "Choose PIN (Windows Hello). A Hello PIN can be configured and entered using the existing keyboard and unlocks a credential bound to that device. Facial recognition requires a compatible infrared camera, and fingerprint recognition requires a compatible reader, neither available in this scenario. The Security key category requires a physical authenticator that the stem explicitly says is unavailable; seeing a category in Settings does not mean its hardware is present. A device-bound PIN is not simply the remotely reusable account password, and choosing it does not by itself make every login an independent two-factor transaction.",
