      "explanation": "1. Microsoft Authenticator app can send push notifications to approve sign-in attempts for both local and Microsoft accounts. → No\n2. You can use the Microsoft Authenticator app to login if you forget your password. → Yes\n3. Microsoft Authenticator app generates time-based one-time passwords as part of the multi-factor authentication process. → Yes\n\nMicrosoft Authenticator supports cloud-account sign-in approvals, passwordless methods where configured, and TOTP generation for compatible services. It does not natively approve ordinary local Windows account logons merely by being installed on a phone. A forgotten password may be addressed through a previously configured passwordless or recovery flow that accepts the app; it is not a universal recovery bypass for any account. TOTP codes use a secret and time, so code generation itself can work offline, whereas push delivery requires connectivity. Availability depends on account setup, registration, and organizational policy.",
