      "question": "For each statement about Device Manager and Disk Management, select True or False.",
      "explanation": "1. Setting up a new drive is done through Disk Management. → Yes\n2. Freeing up disk space for a slow running computer is done through Disk Management. → No\n3. Manually updating drivers can be done through the Device Manager. → Yes\n\nDisk Management shows disks and their partition/volume state, including an uninitialized disk, an offline volume, or a missing drive letter. It is the most specific listed tool for checking why an attached drive is absent from File Explorer. Device Manager is useful if the hardware itself does not enumerate. Computer Management contains Disk Management but is a broader container, while Services controls background services. Do not initialize or format an existing data disk merely because it is missing from Explorer; first determine its state and protect its data. Disk Management manages disks, partitions, volumes, drive letters, and formatting. It does not create System Restore points or delete temporary files as a cleanup operation. System Protection manages restore points, while Storage Sense or Disk Cleanup addresses temporary files and related removable data. Shrinking a volume creates unallocated disk space for another volume; it does not increase free space within the original filesystem. These utilities have distinct responsibilities despite all relating to storage in a broad sense. Device Manager is the hardware-driver management interface. Update Driver offers automatic search and browsing for a compatible local package; a manufacturer’s official support site may supply a package Windows does not find. Roll Back Driver returns to the available previous driver and is appropriate when a new driver caused a failure, as the touchpad screenshot’s Driver tab illustrates. It is not an unrestricted selector for every historical version. Disabling stops the device and uninstalling removes its current device configuration; neither specifically selects the prior driver. Apps and Features and the Store manage applications instead.",
