      "question": "For each of the following statements regarding types of networks, select Yes if the\nstatement is true and No if it is false.",
      "explanation": "1. An extranet gives external partners unrestricted access to all internal resources. → No\n2. An intranet serves internal organizational users behind controlled network access. → Yes\n3. The Internet is a widely used example of a public network. → Yes\n\nAn intranet serves an organization’s authorized internal users and can run over Internet-connected infrastructure with controlled access. An extranet extends selected resources to authorized partners or customers; it does not grant unrestricted access to everything internal. The Internet is the familiar public network. A guest segment normally isolates visitors from internal resources while allowing Internet access. These business-network design labels should not be confused with Windows Public, Private, and Domain firewall profiles, which describe trust and firewall policy on an endpoint.",
