      "explanation": "1. The main circuit board connecting all components, providing expansion slots. → Motherboard\n2. Volatile memory used to hold data and instructions actively being processed by the CPU. → RAM (Random Access Memory)\n3. Non-volatile storage used for long-term data retention and OS installation. → Physical Storage (SSD/HDD)\n\nThe CPU executes program instructions and performs general arithmetic and logic. An APU integrates CPU and graphics-processing functions rather than replacing all storage or system RAM. RAM provides volatile high-speed workspace for active programs, while SSD/HDD storage retains the operating system and files across power loss. The motherboard connects the components and provides sockets, slots, and support circuitry; the GPU renders graphics. These functions cooperate, but temporary memory, permanent storage, and instruction execution are not interchangeable even when several functions are integrated on one chip.",
