      "question": "A manufacturer driver was delivered through Windows Update last week. Where in Windows Settings should a technician first check its installation history?",
      "explanation": "Windows Update > Update history is the direct Settings location for reviewing installation history, including driver-update entries when supplied through Windows Update. It can also lead to removal of eligible Windows updates. It is not a universal way to roll back every installed device driver; use Device Manager for an available driver rollback. Task Manager Startup controls app launch, System Information reports hardware/software details, and Local Security Policy configures rules rather than showing Windows Update installation history. Check timestamps and package names before removing anything.",
