      "question": "When configuring the initial Windows installation, the user is presented with the option to choose between a Microsoft Account and a local account. Which is the main benefit of choosing a Microsoft Account? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "A personal Microsoft account is a cloud identity used across supported Microsoft services and Windows devices. It enables eligible settings synchronization and OneDrive access when the relevant options are enabled and connectivity is available. It is not inherently a paid subscription, a VPN requirement, or an administrator privilege level. Local accounts do not automatically synchronize between computers, and organizational domain accounts use a different identity authority. Previously established Windows sign-in can work offline, so cloud identity does not mean an Internet connection is required for every subsequent sign-in.",
