      "question": "A standard user tries to install a new desktop application and receives a prompt requiring administrative credentials. This situation confirms which characteristic of a Standard User account? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "User Account Control separates routine execution from administrative elevation. With default prompt behavior, an administrator generally consents to elevation, while a standard user supplies valid administrator credentials for an operation that requires them. The requested process receives administrative privileges; the standard account is not permanently promoted. UAC also applies to installers and protected file or configuration changes, not only the Settings application. It is neither antivirus nor MFA and does not grant unrestricted domain-wide rights. Per-user applications that need no elevation are a different case.",
