      "type": "drag_drop",
      "question": "A consultant is explaining the various Microsoft cloud offerings to a client. Move each\nservice from the list on the left to the correct service description on the right.\n\n : An organization-wide platform used for team sites and collaborative document\nmanagement.\n : A subscription service providing a full suite of cloud-based applications,\nincluding Word, Excel, and Outlook.\n : A virtual desktop solution that streams a personalized cloud PC experience to\nvarious devices.\n : A digital note-taking application designed to organize information using sections\nand pages, similar to a physical notebook.",
      "explanation": "1. An organization-wide platform used for team sites and collaborative document management. → SharePoint\n2. A subscription service providing a full suite of cloud-based applications, including Word, Excel, and Outlook. → Microsoft 365\n3. A virtual desktop solution that streams a personalized cloud PC experience to various devices. → Windows 365\n4. A digital note-taking application designed to organize information using sections and pages, similar to a physical notebook. → OneNote\n\nMicrosoft 365 is the productivity-application and cloud-service suite. OneNote is the digital notebook organized into notebooks, sections, and pages. SharePoint provides organization sites and document libraries for collaboration. Windows 365 provides a hosted Cloud PC that users access from supported client devices or browsers. A Cloud PC is not simply a OneNote notebook or a license for local Office applications. The services can integrate, but each mapping follows the distinctive purpose rather than the shared fact that they all use Microsoft cloud infrastructure.",
