      "chapter": "aplicatii-periferice",
      "type": "dropdown",
      "question": "A user reports intermittent loss of Internet access, suspecting an issue with their\nWi-Fi connection to the local router. Evaluate the troubleshooting actions and complete\nthe statements by selecting the correct option from each drop-down list.\n\nTo verify the device has a valid IP address and troubleshoot DNS issues, the technician\nshould run the \n[1]\n command.\nTo confirm the connection status and signal quality of the wireless access point, the\nuser should verify the \n[2]\n.\nIf the device is assigned a 169.254.x.x IP address, you should run the \n[3]\n command to\nattempt a new address acquisition from the DHCP server.",
      "explanation": "1. Blank [1] → ipconfig /all\n2. Blank [2] → Wi-Fi connection status and signal strength\n3. Blank [3] → ipconfig /renew\n\nUse ipconfig to inspect basic IP addressing and ipconfig /all for detailed adapter, DHCP, and DNS configuration. ipconfig /renew requests a DHCP lease; /release relinquishes it; /flushdns clears the local DNS resolver cache rather than obtaining an address. Check the wired cable or enabled Wi-Fi connection as appropriate, and ping the default gateway to test the local router path. A failed ping is not conclusive if ICMP is filtered. Formatting disks, changing wallpaper, or disabling all security does not diagnose network connectivity; restart network equipment only when authorized.",
