      "chapter": "securitate-dispozitiv",
      "type": "single",
      "question": "A user wants to perform an action that modifies system-wide files, such as deleting\nfiles from the Windows directory or changing core system configurations. Which specific\ntype of account is required to execute these high-level administrative tasks on a\nWindows 11 Home computer? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "An administrator account can authorize elevated changes to protected system settings, files, and drivers. A standard account normally lacks those privileges and must obtain approved elevation when required. Microsoft account describes the identity source, not automatic administrator status; Guest is more restricted, and a domain identity is not a Windows Home requirement. Even administrators are not literally unrestricted: UAC, ACLs, protected services, policy, and encryption keys still matter. Use a standard account for routine work and elevate only for authorized administration.",
