      "explanation": "Personalization contains Windows appearance controls such as background, Colors/theme, and Taskbar settings. On Windows 11, Taskbar behaviors includes left or center icon alignment. That changes icon alignment, not the entire taskbar’s screen edge. Start-folder selection controls shortcut folders rather than alignment, and Display resolution changes pixels rather than the theme. Accessibility addresses assistive presentation/input controls, while System handles display and power among other hardware-related settings. Choose the appearance settings for background, dark mode, and alignment.",
