      "explanation": "A conversational assistant such as Copilot can generate troubleshooting instructions, explain settings locations, draft text, or suggest programming code from a prompt. These are informational/generative capabilities and do not require pretending the assistant physically replaces a component or reconnects a cable. Direct device actions depend on an available supported integration, permissions, and user authorization. Generating instructions is not proof that the suggested commands have executed or that a diagnosis is correct. Validate advice before making administrative or destructive changes; Copilot is not an automatic bypass of UAC or management policy.",
