      "type": "single",
      "question": "A user accidentally overwrote a critical content in a Word document stored on a local NTFS folder that has \"File History\" or \"Shadow Copies\" enabled. The user needs to restore the document to the state it was in yesterday morning. Which tab in the file's Properties dialog box should the user access to locate and restore this specific backup? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "File History periodically copies covered personal files to a configured external drive or network location, retaining earlier versions that can be restored after accidental modification or deletion. Previous Versions can expose versions supplied by supported backup or shadow-copy mechanisms when those exist. System Restore targets system state, not document versioning; the Recycle Bin helps with some deletions but not an overwritten saved file. BitLocker protects confidentiality and Disk Cleanup removes files. Prior versions must have been captured before the incident; enabling backup afterward cannot recreate yesterday’s contents.",
      "options": [
        "Security",
        "Details",
        "Previous Versions",
        "Sharing"
      ],
      "correct": 2
