      "explanation": "Map Network Drive associates a drive letter such as Z: with an accessible SMB share, for example \\\\FileServer01\\Projects. It offers a familiar recurring entry in File Explorer without copying the shared contents locally. Workplace Join concerns device identity registration, Storage Spaces pools disks, and BitLocker encrypts storage. A local copy can become stale and does not preserve live access to the shared folder. The mapping still depends on connectivity, valid credentials, and permissions; it does not turn remote storage into an independent physical local disk.",
