      "explanation": "A genuinely new, empty uninitialized disk must first be initialized with a supported partition style, normally GPT on modern systems. Then create a volume, format it with a filesystem, and assign a drive letter or a folder mount point. A drive letter is not mandatory if an NTFS mount point is used, and data volumes as well as OS volumes need a usable filesystem. Optimization does not initialize a disk. If an existing disk unexpectedly appears uninitialized, stop and investigate before writing a new partition table because it may contain recoverable data.",
