      "id": "dcm-482",
      "chapter": "securitate-dispozitiv",
      "type": "single",
      "question": "An administrator changes the NTFS permissions on a parent folder named \"Confidential\". They want to ensure that these new restrictions immediately apply to all existing subfolders and files inside \"Confidential\", overriding any previous settings. Which option in the Advanced Security Settings must be selected? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "Replace all child object permission entries with inheritable permission entries from this object propagates the intended parent permissions to descendants, replacing existing child permission entries as the option indicates. This is stronger and more disruptive than simply enabling future inheritance; review the impact and required privileges before applying it. Changing the owner does not itself assign the desired data ACL, auditing records access rather than granting it, and converting inherited entries to explicit entries can preserve rather than replace divergent settings. Permission propagation is not a substitute for verifying effective access afterward.",
      "options": [
        "Replace all child object permission entries with inheritable permission entries from this object.",
        "Disable inheritance and convert permissions to explicit permissions.",
        "Enable auditing for object access.",
        "Change the owner of the object."
      ],
      "correct": 0
