      "type": "single",
      "question": "A consultant needs to secure sensitive data stored on a removable USB flash drive. The data must be encrypted so that if the drive is lost or stolen, the information remains unreadable to unauthorized users. Which Windows feature is specifically designed for this purpose? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "BitLocker encrypts a volume to protect its stored data when a device or drive is lost or stolen. BitLocker To Go is the removable-data-drive application of this technology. EFS instead encrypts selected files on NTFS; NTFS permissions enforce access checks but do not encrypt the underlying sectors. A firewall filters network traffic, and Secure Boot checks the boot trust chain, neither replacing encryption. BitLocker is not limited to domain-joined devices; enablement depends on edition and hardware, and recovery information must be saved separately and securely.",
