      "question": "A network administrator needs to verify the path that data packets take to reach a\nremote web server and identify where the connection is experiencing latency (delays).\nWhich command-line tool should they use?",
      "explanation": "ping tests whether a destination responds to ICMP echo, while tracert uses TTL-limited probes to reveal responding hops and their measured round-trip times. ipconfig reports local addressing, and ipconfig /renew requests a DHCP lease. nslookup queries DNS rather than tracing the path. A nonresponse can result from filtering or rate limiting, and a slow intermediate probe does not necessarily prove application traffic is delayed there. Use the tool matching the requested evidence and interpret it alongside connectivity and service tests.",
