      "question": "For each statement regarding Windows Storage Sense, select Yes if the statement is true\nand No if the statement is false.",
      "explanation": "1. Storage Sense requires the user to manually run the tool every time disk space is low. → No\n2. Storage Sense can automatically delete files in the Recycle Bin that have been there for over 30 days. → Yes\n3. Storage Sense can be configured to delete temporary files that apps are not using. → Yes\n\nStorage Sense can run automatically to remove eligible temporary files and manage Recycle Bin retention according to configured thresholds, including 30 days. It is not limited to a manual cleanup every time space is low. Disk Cleanup can perform a manual cleanup but is not the Settings automation feature requested. Optimize Drives handles storage layout/TRIM maintenance rather than deleting old Recycle Bin contents, and System Restore manages restore points. Review configured categories because automatic cleanup intentionally removes data and should not be used as a backup strategy.",
