      "chapter": "acces-date",
      "type": "drag_drop",
      "question": "Match each Microsoft cloud service to its primary purpose.\n\n : Personal cloud storage integrated into File Explorer for backing up Desktop, Documents, and Pictures.\n : A collaboration platform primarily used for team communication, meetings, and file sharing.\n : A web-based platform used by organizations to create websites and manage content/documents.",
      "explanation": "1. Personal cloud storage integrated into File Explorer for backing up Desktop, Documents, and Pictures. → OneDrive\n2. A collaboration platform primarily used for team communication, meetings, and file sharing. → Microsoft Teams\n3. A web-based platform used by organizations to create websites and manage content/documents. → SharePoint\n\nAzure provides a broad cloud-computing platform, including virtual machines and application hosting. SharePoint supplies organization sites and document libraries; Teams focuses on chat, meetings, and collaboration, often using SharePoint for channel files. OneDrive provides individual file storage and synchronization. Microsoft 365 is the productivity-service suite rather than just a storage directory. Their functions overlap through integration, but the mappings use the defining requirement: infrastructure, team document sites, live communication, personal files, or a productivity subscription.",
