      "type": "drag_drop",
      "question": "Match the Device Manager icon or symbol to its correct meaning.\n\n : The device has a problem, a configuration error, or a missing driver.\n : The device has been manually disabled by an administrator or user.\n : The device is working properly.",
      "explanation": "1. The device has a problem, a configuration error, or a missing driver. → Yellow Triangle with Exclamation Mark\n2. The device has been manually disabled by an administrator or user. → Small Down Arrow\n3. The device is working properly. → No extra symbol (Standard Icon)\n\nA yellow warning triangle indicates a device problem, such as missing/incompatible drivers or a configuration/resource error; inspect the status/error code for the actual reason. A small downward arrow identifies a disabled device in modern Device Manager. A normal icon without an overlay generally indicates no reported status problem, but is not proof that every real-world function has been tested. These symbols guide diagnosis and should not be confused with a printer queue state, an uninstall action, or a guarantee of physical hardware failure.",
