      "explanation": "1. Hiding filename extensions is a recommended defense against deceptive filenames. → No\n2. Displaying filename extensions helps identify suspicious names, although extensions do not verify file contents. → Yes\n3. Hidden items shows ordinary hidden files and folders; protected OS files have an additional separate visibility setting. → Yes\n\nShowing filename extensions helps reveal deceptive names such as a document-looking executable, although an extension alone cannot validate file contents. Hiding extensions can obscure the real final extension and is not a security defense. Hidden items reveals ordinary hidden files; protected operating-system files have an additional separate display setting. Neither display option changes NTFS permissions or makes it safe to execute a file. Use the view to improve inspection and combine it with source verification and security controls, not as a replacement for malware protection.",
