      "explanation": "1. The **taskkill** command is used to install new software updates. → No\n2. The **ipconfig** command displays the current IP address and network configuration. → Yes\n3. The **ping** command is used to test connectivity to another network device. → Yes\n\ntaskkill terminates processes; it does not install software updates. ipconfig displays local IP/network configuration, and ping sends reachability probes to a target. A successful ping demonstrates an ICMP response, not necessarily that a website or every application service works. Conversely, blocked ICMP can make a live host fail to answer. These commands have distinct purposes, so the correct evaluation is No for update installation, Yes for configuration display, and Yes for a basic connectivity test.",
