      "question": "Which least-privileged ordinary Windows account type should be used for library visitors who must not make administrative system changes? Kiosk policy can impose further restrictions.",
      "explanation": "Use a standard user account for routine work that should not receive administrative control of system-wide security or installation. Administrator, Domain Administrator, and Local System provide far more privilege; a managed service account is intended for services, not an employee desktop. A standard user may still install permitted per-user or Store applications, so account type alone cannot guarantee a complete ban on all new software. Enforce additional application-control, kiosk, or device-management policy when that stricter requirement exists. The built-in Guest account is normally disabled and is not the preferred general modern visitor workflow.",
