      "explanation": "1. You can find and install optional updates directly within the Advanced Options menu of Windows Update. → Yes\n2. The option to remove a recently applied update is located within the Update History section. → Yes\n3. Mandatory updates that are waiting to be installed require active hours to be configured before they will execute. → No\n\nOptional updates are accessible through Windows Update, commonly Advanced options > Optional updates on Windows 11. Update history provides the route to uninstall eligible updates, though not every update can be removed. Active hours primarily helps avoid automatic restarts during the user’s normal work period; it is not a prerequisite for installing required updates, nor a rule that security updates restart only inside active hours. Some drivers install automatically while others are optional, so not every driver package must be manually selected. Managed policies and deadlines can affect restart behavior.",
