      "explanation": "Application is the first Windows log to inspect for an ordinary Word or third-party application crash. System contains events from Windows components, services, and drivers. Security contains audited sign-in and access events when the relevant audit policy is enabled. Setup concerns installation and servicing, while Forwarded Events holds events collected from other computers through configured forwarding. The Event Viewer screenshot shows these categories. Correlate event time, source, and ID with the failure; some applications also have their own logs, so one empty log does not prove no crash occurred.",
