      "question": "During a routine system sweep, Windows Defender intercepts and isolates a file it\nsuspects is malicious.\n\nHowever, your system administrator verifies that the flagged file is actually a safe,\nrequired application experiencing a false positive.\n\nWhat is the correct procedure to resolve this? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "After an authorized investigation verifies a false positive, restore the file through the antimalware product’s quarantine or Protection history interface. Quarantine isolates suspected content without necessarily deleting it permanently. Do not disable all protection or manually hunt for the quarantine storage as a workaround. A second scan can support investigation, but the question says that verification is already complete and asks how to recover the application. If detection repeats, use the approved vendor false-positive process and narrowly scoped exception procedure rather than treating every alert as safe.",
