      "explanation": "Go back under Settings > System > Recovery returns to the previous Windows feature version when the rollback window and required installation files are still available. It generally retains personal files, but applications/drivers installed after upgrading may need reinstallation. System Restore works with restore points rather than serving as the same feature-version rollback, and Reset reinstalls Windows while removing applications according to its options. Update history is mainly for installed servicing packages. Back up first, and do not delete the previous installation files if rollback is still required.",
