      "question": "You need to set up an automated backup for a specific local directory (e.g.,\nE:\\Work\\Manuals) on a Windows 11 machine. The backup must run every 15 minutes, must not\ndepend on an active internet connection, and should exclusively back up this single\nfolder while allowing for the restoration of previous file versions.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate configuration to achieve this? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "File History is the appropriate listed personal-file versioning tool: configure an external or reachable network target, include the required folder in a covered library, set the requested supported interval, and exclude other covered locations if only that folder must be backed up. A local target supports backup without Internet; a network target still needs local-network connectivity. File History is not a real-time guarantee if the target is unavailable. OneDrive synchronization needs connectivity to upload changes, System Restore protects system state, and a system image is not the requested frequent single-folder version history.",
