      "question": "What is the main difference between Share Permissions and NTFS Permissions? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "SMB share permissions apply when the folder is accessed through its network share; the standard share levels are Read, Change, and Full Control. NTFS file and folder permissions apply to filesystem access both locally and through the share, with levels such as Read & execute and Modify. For network access, the requested action must be allowed by both layers after each layer is evaluated. For a direct local path, share permissions do not participate. The gate-and-office analogy refers to these two layers, not encryption technologies such as EFS.",
