      "explanation": "1. The right to see the list of files within a folder. → List folder / read data\n2. The right to change security settings for other users. → Change permissions\n3. The right to pass through a parent folder to reach a subfolder. → Traverse folder / execute file\n\nList folder/read data permits enumerating directory entries when applied to a folder, while Change permissions authorizes editing its ACL. Traverse folder/execute file concerns passing through a directory path or executing a file according to the object type. Take ownership is distinct from both listing and directly changing permissions. Many users have Bypass traverse checking, so lack of a traverse grant alone does not always prevent access to a known permitted child path. Scope advanced entries carefully to this folder, subfolders, or files rather than assuming one checkbox means the same action on every object.",
