      "question": "To create a secure \"Drop Box\" (where users can deposit files but cannot see what others have deposited), which type of permissions must be used? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "A drop-box arrangement needs granular advanced NTFS ACLs with carefully scoped create/traverse rights but without general listing, reading others’ files, or deletion rights. Basic Modify is too broad because it ordinarily includes reading and deleting. Share Full Control alone cannot implement that per-object distinction, and Public sharing is not the right design. An unchecked right is not the same as explicit Deny: other memberships may still allow it. Scope List folder/read data separately for folders and created files, and account for creator-owner entries so depositors can complete writes without seeing others’ content.",
