      "explanation": "Take ownership is the advanced right that allows an authorized identity to become the owner of a file or folder. An owner normally can repair the discretionary ACL, which can then grant the data access needed. This is not the same as directly having Change permissions or Modify. Taking ownership does not automatically remove Deny entries, decrypt EFS data, execute every file, or bypass all security. Full control includes ownership/security-management rights, while ordinary read or write rights do not inherently include ownership changes.",
