      "type": "single",
      "question": "Lockout Situation: The Administrator accidentally set NTFS \"Deny - Full Control\" for the Everyone group on a critical folder, affecting himself as well. Now no one has access. Which listed authorized recovery workflow can repair the ACL? (Choose one)",
      "explanation": "When authorized recovery of an inaccessible NTFS folder is required, taking ownership can enable ACL repair, after which the administrator must grant suitable data permissions. Ownership does not automatically remove every Deny or decrypt EFS content. Deleted owners do not always make access impossible if another identity already has permission-management rights. Safe Mode and CHKDSK do not override an ACL, and changing share permissions does not fix a direct local NTFS denial. Conversion to FAT32 is destructive and not an appropriate recovery shortcut. This is an authorized security-repair workflow, not a universal requirement for every denied folder.",
