      "id": "dcm-612",
      "chapter": "securitate-dispozitiv",
      "type": "drag_drop",
      "question": "Match the Antimalware term with its definition.\n\n : Constant monitoring of the system in the background.\n : A secure area where suspicious files are isolated.\n : A legitimate file incorrectly identified as malware.",
      "explanation": "1. Constant monitoring of the system in the background. → Real-time Protection\n2. A secure area where suspicious files are isolated. → Quarantine\n3. A legitimate file incorrectly identified as malware. → False Positive\n\nReal-time protection monitors activity as files are opened or executed, while current security intelligence helps recognize known threats. Quarantine isolates suspicious content so it cannot run normally and may permit authorized restoration after a false-positive investigation; Delete removes the file rather than merely isolating it. An exclusion deliberately reduces scanning coverage for its scope and should be narrowly justified. No Threats Found is not a promise of future immunity. After a serious compromise, contain and eradicate the threat, then change exposed credentials from a trusted device; do not treat a clean scan as a complete incident response.",
