      "type": "dropdown",
      "question": "Evaluate the following statements about Spyware. Select Yes if the statement is true and No if it is false.",
      "explanation": "1. The primary goal of spyware is to collect personal information and transmit it to a third party without consent. → Yes\n2. Spyware is designed to be highly visible, frequently alerting the user of its presence. → No\n3. A Keylogger is a type of spyware that records every keystroke made by the user. → Yes\n\nSpyware covertly collects information or activity without authorization. A keylogger records keyboard input, screen capture records displayed content, and credential theft can extract saved browser or application secrets. Ransomware instead primarily extorts access to or confidentiality of data, although some attacks combine theft and encryption. Spyware generally tries to avoid notice; it is not designed to keep helpfully announcing its presence. “Every keystroke” and “completely invisible” are simplified descriptions of intent, not guarantees that a particular implementation captures all secure input or cannot be detected.",
