      "question": "Match the terms related to Denial of Service attacks.\n\n : A network of compromised computers controlled by an attacker.\n : An individual infected computer participating in a DDoS attack.\n : The process of filtering out malicious traffic before it hits the server.",
      "explanation": "1. A network of compromised computers controlled by an attacker. → Botnet\n2. An individual infected computer participating in a DDoS attack. → Zombie / Bot\n3. The process of filtering out malicious traffic before it hits the server. → Scrubbing\n\nA botnet is a collection of systems controlled by an attacker, often through compromise. An individual participating machine is a bot or zombie. Scrubbing filters malicious traffic at a suitable upstream or mitigation service before forwarding legitimate traffic to the protected service. Phishing manipulates a person and does not name a traffic-filtering stage. Distributed attacks can involve botnets but also reflection/amplification sources; the mapping describes the supplied botnet scenario rather than requiring every DDoS to use identical malware on every sender.",
