      "explanation": "Ransomware typically encrypts files or locks access, then demands payment for restoration; modern incidents may also steal data and threaten disclosure. Keylogging and quiet password collection are spyware behaviors, while unwanted advertisements characterize adware. Physical hardware destruction is not the defining goal. Paying the demand does not guarantee recovery, and decrypting files alone would not prove the system is trustworthy. Containment, investigation, clean recovery, and independent backups are the appropriate operational context for recognizing this threat.",
