      "explanation": "1. An older analog video-only connector that does not transmit audio. → VGA\n2. A versatile digital interface that can simultaneously transmit video, data, and power. → USB Type-C\n3. A common digital interface used to transmit both high-definition video and audio, frequently used for televisions. → HDMI\n4. A digital display interface originally developed by VESA, often used for high refresh rate PC gaming monitors. → DisplayPort\n\nUSB Type-C is the reversible connector used for compatible power and data connections; video and charging capabilities depend on the port, device, and cable. VGA is the legacy analog video interface, usually with fifteen contacts and retaining screws. DisplayPort is a digital PC-display interface supporting features such as multi-stream transport where implemented. HDMI is the common digital audio/video interface on TVs and game consoles. These purposes distinguish the mappings; neither a separate audio license for DisplayPort nor universal USB-C video support should be assumed.",
