      "type": "dropdown",
      "question": "For each statement about managing applications and services in Windows 11, select True or False.",
      "explanation": "1. You can disable applications from automatically opening when Windows starts by using the Startup apps tab in Task Manager. → Yes\n2. Ending a background process in Task Manager will permanently uninstall the application from your computer. → No\n3. The Services tab in Task Manager allows you to stop and restart background system services. → Yes\n\nTask Manager’s Performance view shows live CPU, memory, disk, and network activity. Startup apps controls whether eligible apps launch automatically at sign-in, not whether they are installed. App history displays usage information and does not uninstall desktop applications. Processes/End task terminates execution, while Services permits authorized control of services such as starting, stopping, or restarting them. Ending a process is temporary and does not remove the installed application or guarantee it will not restart through a service or startup mechanism.",
