      "question": "In Windows 11, you want to change the display resolution and increase the scale of text and apps because they appear too small on your high-resolution monitor.\n\nWhere should you navigate to make these changes?",
      "explanation": "Scale changes the displayed size of text, applications, and other interface elements while retaining the chosen output pixel resolution. Display resolution selects the pixel dimensions of the desktop signal; orientation rotates it between landscape and portrait; refresh rate controls update frequency. The screenshot’s Scale row explicitly describes changing the size of text, apps, and other items. These are separate controls under System > Display, not interchangeable ways of enlarging everything. Available values depend on the connected display, graphics driver, and Windows version.",
