      "explanation": "1. Blank [1] → Read and Execute\n2. Blank [2] → Modify\n3. Blank [3] → Full Control\n\nRead permits opening data without editing, and Read & execute additionally permits execution. Read plus Write allows common viewing/creation/editing operations but does not inherently grant Delete. Modify combines ordinary read, write, execute, and deletion. Full control adds security-management capabilities such as changing permissions and taking ownership. These are bundled rights; advanced ACLs can be more selective and applicable Deny entries can limit specific requests. The question compares the named permission bundles, not an assurance that all compound application workflows will succeed with one narrowly granted right.",
