      "explanation": "1. Tests the basic network reachability of a device using an IP address or domain name. → ping\n2. Displays the route and measures transit delays of packets across an IP network. → tracert\n3. Forces a manual refresh of local and Active Directory network security settings. → gpupdate /force\n4. Displays all current TCP/IP network configuration values, including the MAC address. → ipconfig /all\n\ngpupdate /force requests immediate reapplication of both user and computer Group Policy on the local device; some extensions still require sign-out or restart, and domain contact must be available where needed. gpresult reports resulting policy rather than applying it: /R gives summary information, /V verbose details, and /H writes an HTML report with a filename. /R does not mean remote; remote targeting uses /S. Refreshing System Information or reloading a local console does not cause domain GPO settings to be reapplied.",
