      "chapter": "acces-date",
      "type": "drag_drop",
      "question": "Move each service or storage term from the list on the left to its correct description on the right.\n\n : Microsoft's cloud storage service built directly into Windows 11 File Explorer.\n : A subscription service that provides Microsoft Office applications and additional cloud storage.\n : A physical local network storage solution accessible by multiple users in an office.\n : A cloud-based service that streams a full personalized Windows desktop to any device.",
      "explanation": "1. Microsoft's cloud storage service built directly into Windows 11 File Explorer. → OneDrive\n2. A subscription service that provides Microsoft Office applications and additional cloud storage. → Microsoft 365\n3. A physical local network storage solution accessible by multiple users in an office. → NAS (Network Attached Storage)\n4. A cloud-based service that streams a full personalized Windows desktop to any device. → Windows 365\n\nTeams is the communication/collaboration hub for chat and meetings, with integrated shared documents. SharePoint supplies sites and document libraries, and OneDrive focuses on individual file synchronization and sharing. Windows 365 streams a hosted Cloud PC, while Microsoft 365 is the broader productivity subscription suite. A NAS is physical network-attached storage on a local network, not itself Microsoft cloud storage. Exchange primarily supplies messaging and calendaring. Choose the defining need rather than assuming every service that stores files is interchangeable or that a Cloud PC is simply an Office application.",
