      "explanation": "Windows Pro is the normal minimum general-purpose Windows client edition supporting an on-premises Active Directory domain join and domain Group Policy. Enterprise and Education also support these capabilities, while Home does not. S mode restricts application installation and is not an edition that adds domain-join rights. A Home computer can still access some resources with suitable credentials, but that is not equivalent to becoming an AD DS domain member. For a missing domain-join option, check the installed edition before changing accounts or credentials.",
