      "question": "You are trying to connect a new Bluetooth headset to your Windows 11 laptop. The headset is fully charged and in pairing mode, but the laptop does not detect it in the \"Add a device\" window.\n\nWhat is the most likely first step you should verify in the Windows 11 Settings app?",
      "explanation": "Bluetooth discovery requires Bluetooth enabled on the laptop and the headset placed in pairing/discovery mode, within range and not locked into another connection. When the stem already confirms the laptop radio is enabled but does not mention headset pairing mode, check the headset’s pairing mode first. When the headset is charged and in pairing mode, verify the Windows Bluetooth toggle. Driver work or Windows updates may be later steps, but the simplest unverified radio/pairing prerequisite should be checked before assuming a software fault or interference.",
