      "type": "single",
      "question": "A new USB printer is not printing on a Windows 11 PC. The printer is detected in Device Manager, and its Properties status confirms that a required compatible device driver is not installed. Which listed action should you take to address that reported driver problem?",
      "explanation": "Install or update the correct compatible printer driver, using the manufacturer’s official package or another approved Windows driver source. The stem explicitly reports that the required driver is missing, so a driver action addresses the diagnosed fault. Replacing the cable or changing ports is appropriate for a suspected physical connection failure, but the printer has already enumerated and the stated problem is its driver. Reinstalling the whole operating system is disproportionate. Verify the exact printer model, Windows version, and architecture, complete any required restart or reconnection, and then test printing. A generic warning icon alone would not establish this diagnosis.",
      "options": [
        "Update the device driver.",
        "Replace the USB cable.",
        "Plug the printer into a different USB port.",
        "Reinstall the Windows operating system."
      ],
