      "question": "For each statement about network profiles in Windows 11, select True or False.",
      "explanation": "1. The Public profile uses restrictive discovery defaults suitable for untrusted networks. → Yes\n2. Private is the recommended profile for an unknown coffee-shop hotspot. → No\n3. Private permits trusted discovery and file sharing when their sharing settings and firewall rules are enabled. → Yes\n\nUse Public for untrusted networks such as an airport, coffee shop, or hotel; its restrictive defaults discourage network discovery and inbound sharing. Use Private for a trusted home or non-domain office network where discovery and sharing are intentionally permitted. Private does not itself grant file permissions or guarantee that every sharing switch is enabled. Domain is automatically selected when Windows authenticates the network to an AD domain, not merely because an office is trusted. These are firewall/trust profiles, not proof that a network is encrypted, safe, or reachable from the Internet.",
