      "type": "single",
      "question": "A user recently purchased a Windows 11 laptop and cannot install a third-party web browser downloaded from the internet. The system only allows app installations from the Microsoft Store.\n\nWhat is the most likely cause of this limitation?",
      "explanation": "Windows in S mode restricts conventional application installation to approved Microsoft Store sources, which explains the explicit verified-apps-only message. It is not Safe Mode, a diagnostic startup environment, or Tablet Mode, a user-interface feature. UAC controls elevation rather than imposing a Store-only software model, and standard users can run some per-user desktop installers. Switching out of S mode is a separate supported policy/account decision and may be one-way; do not recommend bypassing organizational controls simply to install a browser. In Windows 11, S mode applies to the Home edition.",
