      "explanation": "Delivery Optimization can download eligible update content from other PCs, including configured local-network peers, reducing repeated Internet downloads. It still needs appropriate policy, peer availability, and content access; it does not guarantee that no data comes from Microsoft. WSUS is a different managed update-distribution/approval infrastructure rather than the peer feature described. Active hours manages restart timing, and Optional updates selects packages. Configure the sharing scope to the organization’s requirements and do not assume unrestricted Internet-peer sharing is necessary for local peer delivery.",
