      "question": "A user has limited vision and needs the text and images on their Windows 11 screen to be significantly larger. They want a tool that acts like a digital magnifying glass following their mouse cursor.\n\nWhich Accessibility feature should they use?",
      "explanation": "Magnifier temporarily enlarges part or all of the screen and can follow the pointer or focus, which suits a user who needs a closer view while reading particular content. Changing text size affects text more broadly and is not the same as a movable magnifying view. Narrator speaks content rather than enlarging it; font settings manage installed fonts. Contrast themes and captions address other needs. The correct choice follows the requested temporary visual magnification, not a permanent change of every font or application layout.",
