      "chapter": "acces-date",
      "type": "single",
      "question": "You want to completely remove a desktop application and all its associated files from your Windows 11 computer.\n\nWhat is the proper method?",
      "explanation": "Use the application’s supported Uninstall entry, for example from Installed apps/Apps & features or Programs and Features. Some Start context-menu entries also provide Uninstall. This invokes the app’s removal process rather than simply deleting its executable folder or shortcut. Manual folder or Registry deletion can leave services, registrations, and dependencies inconsistent. Ending a task stops execution only, and CHKDSK checks a disk rather than uninstalling software. Even a proper uninstaller can intentionally retain user data or settings, so complete removal of every trace is not guaranteed.",
