      "explanation": "Copilot availability and Windows integration depend on the supported OS/app version, rollout period, account, region, and organizational policy. The historical in-box Copilot experience first appeared on supported Windows 11 builds and later some Windows 10 devices; later standalone and web experiences changed that distribution model. It is not universally limited to paid Microsoft 365 subscriptions, Microsoft-only applications, or grammatically complete prompts. Task View organizes windows, Widgets presents feeds, and File Explorer manages files. A taskbar entry is version/configuration dependent rather than an immutable component of every Windows 11 installation.",
