      "question": "Read the following statements regarding the different update types found in Update History. Choose True or False for each.",
      "explanation": "1. Third-party and device manufacturer drivers can be installed through Windows Driver updates. → Yes\n2. Security vulnerabilities are occasionally patched by installing feature updates. → Yes\n3. A service pack is a single package that bundles multiple past hotfixes, patches, and updates. → Yes\n\nWindows Update can distribute driver packages from hardware manufacturers, not only drivers written by Microsoft. Feature updates introduce or change Windows capabilities and can include security improvements; they are not guaranteed to be security-free. Historically, service packs bundled many earlier fixes and updates into a package. Modern Windows servicing uses feature and cumulative quality updates rather than assuming every release has a service-pack model. Update history categories identify package roles, not the vendor’s identity or a guarantee that optional packages are always present.",
