      "explanation": "Windows 11 groups Narrator, pointer sizing, visual sound alerts, and other assistive controls under Accessibility. Windows 10 commonly used the category name Ease of Access. Select the category matching the operating-system version in the stem rather than treating the two labels as competing features on the same build. Apps manages software, Personalization controls appearance themes, and Windows Update manages servicing. Some related settings have multiple entry points, but Accessibility is the direct category for the stated assistive requirement in Windows 11.",
