      "question": "Identify the type of data transmitted by each port connection. Choose Audio, Video, or Audio & Video from each drop-down menu.\n\nDisplayPort: \n[1]\n\nVGA: \n[2]\n\nHDMI: \n[3]\n\nS/PDIF Optical: \n[4]",
      "explanation": "1. Blank [1] → Audio & Video\n2. Blank [2] → Video\n3. Blank [3] → Audio & Video\n4. Blank [4] → Audio\n\nDisplayPort and HDMI normally carry digital audio and video. VGA carries analog video only, so separate audio is needed. Optical S/PDIF, commonly using a TOSLINK connector, carries digital audio and not a video image. These are interface capabilities, not guarantees that a particular source is sending an audio track or that every sink supports every format. A video-only VGA cable cannot become an audio/video cable by changing a Windows default sound device.",
