      "question": "As an entry-level IT support specialist, you receive a report that an employee's work laptop has a shattered display after falling off a desk. The employee frequently travels between remote and on-site work. After confirming the display is completely broken, what is your best course of action?",
      "explanation": "Document the symptoms, tests, and diagnosis, then escalate the ticket to the authorized next support tier when specialized hardware knowledge, repair authority, or the troubleshooting time limit exceeds Tier 1’s scope. This preserves continuity without making the user start over. Waiting to obtain training delays the immediate fix, while abandoning the ticket or sending the user to a vendor bypasses the internal support process. A broken mobile laptop screen is not permanently solved by prescribing a desktop monitor, and an untrained technician should not attempt an unauthorized panel replacement.",
