      "question": "You are trying to operate an older industrial printer using a USB-to-serial converter on Windows 11. While the device is detected, communication fails. To fix this, you must adjust the serial port settings like baud rate and parity. Under which section in Device Manager do you configure these parameters?",
      "explanation": "A USB-to-serial adapter presents a COM port, so open Ports (COM & LPT), choose the relevant COM device, and inspect its port settings for baud rate, data bits, parity, stop bits, and flow control. Those must match the legacy device’s communication requirements. Print queues concerns print jobs and printer objects, while USB controllers concerns the host USB bus, not the serial protocol settings exposed by the adapter. Display adapters and general system devices are unrelated categories. Some application software also configures these values independently.",
