      "question": "Prepare a 3TB data disk for an ordinary Windows 11 system. Select the partition scheme that exposes its full capacity and the broadly supported Windows file system with metadata journaling. ReFS availability varies by Windows edition and volume role.",
      "explanation": "GPT avoids the approximately 2 TiB addressing limit of MBR with traditional 512-byte logical sectors, exposing the full capacity of the 3 TB disk. NTFS is the broadly supported Windows choice with metadata journaling and file-level security. FAT32 lacks those NTFS security features and has a small individual-file limit; exFAT targets compatibility and lacks NTFS-style journaling/security. ReFS has edition and volume-role restrictions and is not the general default. Partition style and filesystem are separate decisions: GPT alone does not format the volume, and NTFS cannot remove an MBR addressing limit.",
