      "question": "You are unable to access the internet on your workstation. Which command-line utility should you run to verify the local IPv4 or IPv6 configuration?",
      "explanation": "ipconfig displays the local adapter’s assigned IP address, subnet mask, and default gateway; ipconfig /all adds detailed configuration such as DNS servers, DHCP information, and physical addresses. Neither ping nor tracert is the normal command for enumerating local configuration: ping tests reachability, and tracert examines hops. ipconfig /release gives up a DHCP address rather than simply displaying it. nslookup tests DNS queries, and arp examines local neighbor mappings. Choose the display command before changing configuration so the original diagnostic information is preserved.",
      "options": [
        "nslookup",
        "arp",
        "ipconfig",
        "tracert"
      ],
      "correct": 2
