      "explanation": "System > Display is the relevant settings area for display connections and supported wireless-display workflows, and Windows+K commonly opens the Cast connection pane. Both the source and TV/receiver must support a compatible wireless-display technology and configuration. Sound manages audio, Multitasking manages window behaviors such as Snap, and Remote Desktop provides remote-session control; they do not serve as the direct screen-casting selection. A “smart TV” label alone does not prove Miracast or Windows wireless-display compatibility, so check the receiver’s actual capabilities before promising a connection.",
